# System Architecture Diagram
## Customer Churn Intelligence System

---

## 1. High-Level System Architecture

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph USER_LAYER["🖥️ Presentation Layer"]
        UI["Streamlit Web App<br/>(app.py)"]
        CSS["Custom CSS Styling<br/>(Playfair Display + Inter)"]
    end

    subgraph INPUT_LAYER["📋 Input Processing Layer"]
        FORM["Customer Profile Form<br/>(19 Features)"]
        VALIDATE["Input Validation"]
    end

    subgraph ML_LAYER["🤖 ML Inference Layer"]
        ENC["Label Encoders<br/>(encoders.pkl)"]
        SCALE["Standard Scaler<br/>(scaler.pkl)"]
        ORDER["Feature Ordering<br/>(feature_order.pkl)"]
        MODEL["XGBoost Classifier<br/>(final_churn_model.pkl)"]
        THRESH["Optimized Threshold<br/>(threshold.pkl, τ=0.4)"]
    end

    subgraph AGENT_LAYER["🧠 Agentic AI Layer (LangGraph)"]
        RISK["Risk Assessment Node"]
        RAG["RAG Retrieval Node"]
        PLAN["Planning Node"]
    end

    subgraph RAG_LAYER["📚 RAG Knowledge Layer"]
        KB["Retention Knowledge Base<br/>(retention_knowledge.json)"]
        EMB["HuggingFace Embeddings<br/>(all-MiniLM-L6-v2)"]
        FAISS["FAISS Vector Store"]
    end

    subgraph LLM_LAYER["💬 LLM Reasoning Layer"]
        GROQ["Groq API Client"]
        LLAMA["LLaMA 3.3 70B Versatile"]
    end

    subgraph OUTPUT_LAYER["📊 Output Layer"]
        PRED["Churn Prediction Result"]
        STRAT["AI Retention Strategy"]
        CONF["Confidence Score"]
    end

    UI --> FORM
    CSS -.-> UI
    FORM --> VALIDATE
    VALIDATE --> ENC
    ENC --> ORDER
    ORDER --> SCALE
    SCALE --> MODEL
    MODEL -->|"churn_prob"| THRESH
    MODEL -->|"churn_prob"| RISK
    RISK -->|"risk_level + reasons"| RAG
    RAG -->|"strategies + sources"| PLAN
    KB --> EMB
    EMB --> FAISS
    FAISS -.->|"similarity_search(k=3)"| RAG
    PLAN -->|"prompt"| GROQ
    GROQ --> LLAMA
    LLAMA -->|"JSON response"| PLAN
    THRESH --> PRED
    PLAN --> STRAT
    MODEL --> CONF
    PRED --> UI
    STRAT --> UI
    CONF --> UI

    style USER_LAYER fill:#ede9ff,stroke:#7c3aed,stroke-width:2px
    style INPUT_LAYER fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    style ML_LAYER fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#3b82f6,stroke-width:2px
    style AGENT_LAYER fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#22c55e,stroke-width:2px
    style RAG_LAYER fill:#fce7f3,stroke:#ec4899,stroke-width:2px
    style LLM_LAYER fill:#fed7aa,stroke:#f97316,stroke-width:2px
    style OUTPUT_LAYER fill:#e0e7ff,stroke:#6366f1,stroke-width:2px
```

---

## 2. LangGraph Agent Pipeline (Detailed Flow)

```mermaid
graph LR
    START(("▶ START")) --> RISK_NODE

    subgraph RISK_NODE["🔴 Risk Assessment Node"]
        R1["Evaluate churn_prob"]
        R2{"prob > 0.7?"}
        R3{"prob > 0.4?"}
        R4["Risk = High"]
        R5["Risk = Medium"]
        R6["Risk = Low"]
        R7["Check tenure < 6"]
        R8["Check monthly > 80"]
        R9["Append reasons[]"]

        R1 --> R2
        R2 -->|Yes| R4
        R2 -->|No| R3
        R3 -->|Yes| R5
        R3 -->|No| R6
        R4 --> R7
        R5 --> R7
        R6 --> R7
        R7 --> R8
        R8 --> R9
    end

    RISK_NODE --> RETRIEVAL_NODE

    subgraph RETRIEVAL_NODE["🔍 RAG Retrieval Node"]
        S1["Join reasons as query"]
        S2["FAISS similarity_search<br/>(k=3)"]
        S3["Extract strategies[]"]
        S4["Extract sources[]"]

        S1 --> S2
        S2 --> S3
        S3 --> S4
    end

    RETRIEVAL_NODE --> PLANNING_NODE

    subgraph PLANNING_NODE["📝 Planning Node"]
        P1["Build LLM prompt"]
        P2["Call Groq API<br/>(LLaMA 3.3 70B)"]
        P3["Parse JSON response"]
        P4["Fallback on parse error"]

        P1 --> P2
        P2 --> P3
        P3 --> P4
    end

    PLANNING_NODE --> END_NODE(("⏹ END"))

    style RISK_NODE fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#ef4444,stroke-width:2px
    style RETRIEVAL_NODE fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#3b82f6,stroke-width:2px
    style PLANNING_NODE fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#22c55e,stroke-width:2px
```

---

## 3. RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) Pipeline

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph KNOWLEDGE["📖 Knowledge Base"]
        JSON["retention_knowledge.json<br/>(9 strategy entries)"]
    end

    subgraph CONDITIONS["🏷️ Strategy Categories"]
        C1["low_tenure<br/>(2 strategies)"]
        C2["high_charges<br/>(2 strategies)"]
        C3["low_engagement<br/>(2 strategies)"]
        C4["no_support<br/>(1 strategy)"]
        C5["general<br/>(2 strategies)"]
    end

    subgraph EMBEDDING["🔢 Embedding Pipeline"]
        DOC["LangChain Documents<br/>(page_content + metadata)"]
        HF["HuggingFace Embeddings<br/>(all-MiniLM-L6-v2)"]
        VEC["384-dim Vectors"]
    end

    subgraph VECTOR_DB["🗄️ Vector Store"]
        FAISS_DB["FAISS Index<br/>(In-Memory)"]
    end

    subgraph QUERY["🔎 Query Pipeline"]
        REASONS["Agent reasons[]"]
        SEARCH["similarity_search(k=3)"]
        TOP3["Top 3 Matching Strategies"]
    end

    JSON --> C1 & C2 & C3 & C4 & C5
    C1 & C2 & C3 & C4 & C5 --> DOC
    DOC --> HF
    HF --> VEC
    VEC --> FAISS_DB
    REASONS --> SEARCH
    FAISS_DB --> SEARCH
    SEARCH --> TOP3

    style KNOWLEDGE fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    style CONDITIONS fill:#e0e7ff,stroke:#6366f1,stroke-width:2px
    style EMBEDDING fill:#fce7f3,stroke:#ec4899,stroke-width:2px
    style VECTOR_DB fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#22c55e,stroke-width:2px
    style QUERY fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#3b82f6,stroke-width:2px
```

---

## 4. ML Inference Pipeline

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph INPUT["📥 Raw Input (19 Features)"]
        CAT["16 Categorical Features<br/>(Gender, Contract, etc.)"]
        NUM["3 Numerical Features<br/>(Tenure, Monthly, Total)"]
    end

    subgraph ENCODE["🔄 Encoding"]
        LE["LabelEncoder<br/>(per categorical column)"]
    end

    subgraph REORDER["📐 Feature Ordering"]
        FO["feature_order.pkl<br/>(ensures column alignment)"]
    end

    subgraph SCALE["⚖️ Scaling"]
        SS["StandardScaler<br/>(tenure, MonthlyCharges, TotalCharges)"]
    end

    subgraph PREDICT["🎯 Prediction"]
        XGB["XGBoost Classifier"]
        PROBA["predict_proba()"]
        THR["Threshold = 0.4<br/>(Recall-optimized)"]
    end

    subgraph RESULT["📊 Output"]
        PROB["Churn Probability<br/>(0.0 – 1.0)"]
        LABEL["Churn / No Churn"]
        CONF_SCORE["Confidence Score"]
    end

    CAT --> LE
    LE --> FO
    NUM --> FO
    FO --> SS
    SS --> XGB
    XGB --> PROBA
    PROBA --> PROB
    PROB --> THR
    THR --> LABEL
    PROB --> CONF_SCORE

    style INPUT fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    style ENCODE fill:#e0e7ff,stroke:#6366f1,stroke-width:2px
    style REORDER fill:#fed7aa,stroke:#f97316,stroke-width:2px
    style SCALE fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#3b82f6,stroke-width:2px
    style PREDICT fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#22c55e,stroke-width:2px
    style RESULT fill:#fce7f3,stroke:#ec4899,stroke-width:2px
```

---

## 5. End-to-End Data Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant UI as Streamlit UI
    participant Encoder as LabelEncoders
    participant Scaler as StandardScaler
    participant XGBoost as XGBoost Model
    participant LangGraph as LangGraph Agent
    participant FAISS as FAISS VectorStore
    participant Groq as Groq API (LLaMA 3.3)

    User->>UI: Enter 19 customer features
    User->>UI: Click "Run Churn Prediction"
    UI->>UI: Validate inputs
    UI->>Encoder: Encode categorical features
    Encoder-->>UI: Encoded values
    UI->>UI: Reorder features (feature_order.pkl)
    UI->>Scaler: Scale numerical features
    Scaler-->>UI: Scaled DataFrame
    UI->>XGBoost: predict_proba(input)
    XGBoost-->>UI: churn_prob = P(churn)

    UI->>LangGraph: invoke({churn_prob, tenure, monthly})

    Note over LangGraph: Node 1: Risk Assessment
    LangGraph->>LangGraph: Classify risk level (High/Medium/Low)
    LangGraph->>LangGraph: Identify churn reasons

    Note over LangGraph: Node 2: RAG Retrieval
    LangGraph->>FAISS: similarity_search(reasons, k=3)
    FAISS-->>LangGraph: Top 3 strategies + sources

    Note over LangGraph: Node 3: Planning
    LangGraph->>Groq: Send structured prompt
    Groq-->>LangGraph: JSON {risk_summary, recommendations, sources, disclaimer}

    LangGraph-->>UI: final_output

    UI-->>User: Display prediction result
    UI-->>User: Display AI retention strategy
    UI-->>User: Display confidence score
```

---

## 6. Technology Stack

| Layer | Technology | Purpose |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| **Frontend** | Streamlit | Interactive web UI |
| **Styling** | Custom CSS + Google Fonts | Premium UI design |
| **ML Model** | XGBoost | Churn classification |
| **Preprocessing** | Scikit-learn (LabelEncoder, StandardScaler) | Feature encoding & scaling |
| **Serialization** | Joblib | Model & artifact persistence |
| **Agent Framework** | LangGraph (StateGraph) | Multi-node agentic pipeline |
| **Vector Store** | FAISS | In-memory vector similarity search |
| **Embeddings** | HuggingFace (all-MiniLM-L6-v2) | Text → 384-dim vectors |
| **LLM Provider** | Groq API | Fast LLM inference |
| **LLM Model** | LLaMA 3.3 70B Versatile | Strategy generation & reasoning |
| **Knowledge Base** | JSON (retention_knowledge.json) | 9 curated retention strategies |
| **Data Processing** | Pandas, NumPy | DataFrame operations |
| **Environment** | python-dotenv | API key management |

---

## 7. File Structure

```
project/
├── app.py                          # Main Streamlit application (682 lines)
├── retention_knowledge.json        # RAG knowledge base (9 strategies)
├── model_test.py                   # Model validation script
├── requirements.txt                # Python dependencies
├── .env                            # API keys (GROQ_API_KEY)
├── .streamlit/                     # Streamlit configuration
├── notebook_&_otherpkl/
│   ├── CUSTOMER_CHURN_PREDICTION_Gen_AI_Project.ipynb  # Training notebook
│   ├── milestone2_rag_testing.ipynb                    # RAG testing notebook
│   ├── final_churn_model.pkl       # Trained XGBoost model
│   ├── scaler.pkl                  # StandardScaler
│   ├── threshold.pkl               # Optimized threshold (0.4)
│   ├── encoders.pkl                # LabelEncoders (16 columns)
│   └── feature_order.pkl           # Feature column ordering
├── Raw_Dataset/                    # Original CSV data
├── EDA Insights/                   # Exploratory data analysis
├── Report/                         # Project reports
├── images/                         # UI assets
└── README.md                       # Project documentation
```
